{"ts":"2026-08-29T10:29:44.543Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"99c265bc79d0025f861b6e66","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-29T10:29:44.543Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-29T10:29:44.543Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Measured before fixing, by executing the canonical verifier against eighteen probe workflows rather than by reading the code. Eleven returned zero failures on a file the shell would publish unattested from.\n\nHEREDOC (7 shapes). A heredoc body is stdin data and cannot bind a variable in the shell that reads it, but shellScalars read every line as potential source, so `FLAG=--provenance` written inside one was indexed and a later `npm publish $FLAG` borrowed a flag the shell never passed. All seven spellings leaked: plain `<<EOF`, space-separated `<<  EOF`, tab-separated, single- and double-quoted delimiters, tab-stripping `<<-EOF`, and a heredoc written after another redirection (`cat > f <<EOF`). Greptile reported only the space-separated form on pm-beads#88; measurement showed the plain form was equally exposed, so the finding was broader than reported.\n\nUNSET (4 shapes). `unset FLAG` discards a binding, but the map kept it for the rest of the file, so a publish after the unset was audited as attested. Leaked as `unset FLAG`, `echo ready; unset FLAG`, `unset -v FLAG` and `unset OTHER FLAG`.\n\nTwo Greptile P1s did NOT reproduce against this implementation and were closed as already-fixed rather than patched again: escaped operators in a scalar value (`FLAG=--provenance\\;ignored`) are already refused by the post-unescape metacharacter guard, and guarded assignments (`false && FLAG=--provenance`) are already refused by the rule that a line must OPEN with the assignment. Both were reported against pm-beads' older copy of this file.\n\nFIX. Heredoc bodies are located per redirection and excluded from assignment indexing only -- publish detection inside a heredoc is deliberately unchanged, because a heredoc can carry a script that is written to a file and executed later. Both halves fail closed: an unindexed name leaves `$FLAG` unresolved so the publish reads as unattested, and a publish written into a heredoc still has to carry the flag itself.\n\n`unset` is honoured through the tokeniser rather than an anchored whole-line pattern, so `echo ready; unset FLAG` is caught. An unset the parent shell would not actually perform is honoured too, deliberately: dropping a binding can only make a later `$FLAG` unresolve, which FAILS the gate, whereas keeping one the shell discarded is what ships an unattested artifact. The two error directions are not symmetric and only the false alarm is safe.\n\nBecause `unset` gives a binding a lifetime, resolution is now positional: one map per line instead of one per file. That also closes companion item pm-cli-website-1j4o, raised by Sourcery on PR #67 and deferred there as needing position-aware resolution -- an assignment written BELOW a publish no longer attests it.\n\nOne bug was found by the new tests rather than by a bot: the first heredoc pattern matched `<<<word` at its second `<`, reading a herestring as a heredoc delimited by `word` and swallowing the rest of the file as body. That direction is a false alarm rather than a bypass, but it would have failed an attested release. Fixed with a lookbehind; covered by a test.\n\nAll six regression tests were observed FAILING against the reverted behaviour and passing after. The revert was done by neutering the two behaviours in place, keeping every export and signature, so the assertions were measured behaviourally rather than by a compile error. Suite 293 pass / 0 fail; coverage 100/100/100/100; docstring gate clean."}]}],"before_hash":"5f74429ea9b01471c285d536b5664acb04dfcce447fb9d92ecfc8311e92f142d","after_hash":"18df94bc97e6218faa74a11f7184f27eed5cda3c490e5cc3bd8e61b896fc1025","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
